render: return an error when the LF frame of a VarDCT frame is smaller than the frame's LF image.
render_vardct reads the LF coefficients from the LF frame at the frame's own block positions. The
LF frame is sized from the image header, but a frame with a custom size can be larger than the
image, and the reads went past the end of the LF frame (shared_subgrid.rs: coordinate out of
range). Test: lf_frame_size_mismatch (crates/jxl-oxide-tests/tests/lf_frame_size_mismatch.rs).

Upstream: not reported; the code is unchanged at upstream HEAD (c0cc4c7, 2026-08-15).

